## Project Structure

```text
26INF1103P5-2/
├── .env                        # Local environment variables (API keys) — not committed
├── .env.example                # Template for environment variables
├── .gitignore                  # Git ignore file (cache, virtualenv, secrets, env)
├── requirements.txt            # Python package dependencies
├── README.me                   # Project documentation
├── ProjectInitialDetails.md    # Problem statement, users, and business rules
│
├── src/                        # Main application source code
│   ├── main.py                 # Application entry point / main flow orchestration
│   │
│   ├── modules/                # Core building-block functions and integrations
│   │   ├── input_handler.py    # User input, file validation, and PII detection helpers
│   │   ├── logic_manager.py    # Handover business-rule validation
│   │   ├── nvdia_router.py      # LLM (OpenRouter/NVIDIA) communication
│   │   └── llm_prompt.py       # LLM prompt templates
│   │
│   ├── utils/                  # Shared utilities
│   │   ├── __init__.py
│   │   └── logger.py           # Application logger
│   │
│   └── model/                  # Data storage and models
│
├── data/                       # Runtime data
│   └── handovers/              # Handover .txt files loaded by the app
│       └── handover.txt
│
└── test/                       # Automated unit tests
    ├── logic_manager_test.py   # Tests for logic_manager
    └── ai_manager_test.py      # Tests for the AI/LLM portion
```

#installing of library from requirement.txt
- Any library or package you want to use please put into requirement.txt 
so it doesnt break each of our eniviornment when we are trying to intergrate 

- run this command in your CLI ( for python virtual eniviornment users )
py -m pip install -r requirements.txt

- run this command in your cli ( for non venv users )
pip install -r requirements.txt

